    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d191">

                <pb facs="0346" n="284" xml:id="pg284"/>

                <head>No. 186.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Welsh to Mr. Evarts</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1878-08-24"><hi rendition="#italic">August</hi> 24, 1878</date>.
                        (Received September 4.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 132.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your Nos. 33, 55, and 67, and
                    to Mr. Hoppin’s No. 5, relating to certain alleged outrages upon American
                    fishermen committed on the coast of Newfoundland, I have the honor to inform you
                    that I have received a note from Lord Salisbury, inclosing the report of Captain
                    Sulivan, of Her Majesty’s ship Sirius, upon these occurrences. I transmit
                    herewith copies both of Lord Salisbury’s note and of its inclosure.</p>
                <p>I have, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>JOHN WELSH.</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d191-a1.xml" xpointer="d191-a1"/>
                <xi:include href="d191-a2.xml" xpointer="d191-a2"/>
